  "raw_text": "TUBING SCREEN™\nThe Tubing Screen™ is made up of a screen jacket that is perforated tubing with EUE thread. The Tubing Screen™ is designed specifically for wells with high lifting cost that have sand failures. The Tubing Screen™ is run below the pump intake, in place of the perforated pup joint. This allows sand to be filtered out between the tubing and casing.\nCase Study\nWebinar\nOSI shares the knowledge and experience on the following links\nGAS SEPARATOR\nGas shield™ is made up of the diffused intake port which minimizes gas from entering the separator and a large body annulus for reducing fluid velocity, allowing for gas separation. 3 ft intake area with 75 slot screen. 25 ft overall length with 18 ft internally mounted dip tube.\nCHEM TREATMENT\nChem Screen™ is made up of a screen jacket that is placed over perforated J55 EUE Tubing. It is designed specifically for wells with high lifting cost that have sand failures. The Chem Screen™ runs below the pump intake, in place of the perforated pup joint. This allows sand to be filtered out between the tubing and casing.\nVORTEX DESANDER\nThe Screen Vortex Desander™ is designed specifically for wells with high lifting cost that have sand failures. The fluid flows down through the Helix and creates a vortex effect that separates solids via centrifugal force allowing clean liquid to flow up the Dip Tube.\nGUARDIAN SHIELD™\nThe Guardian Shield™ mitigates large slugs of gas from reaching the pump, which helps to stabilize production and reduce the unforeseen interruption. Guardian Shield™ is designed to avoid gas entrance into ESPs by forcing free gas to go around the shroud and protrude through the casing along with fluid passage inside the Guardian Shield™, ensuring cooling of the motor."
}